# The pc platform's gem path test (#1093, docs/platforms.md), played with
# --level 11 --room gem-path (Ace of Space's gem path, the one HOVER room):
# platform/pc/preview.keys's Start and A through the logos and menus to the
# level select (frames 1-514), which picks the level, then the whole hover
# ride, steered with the D-pad (left slows the ride and puts the camera
# lead 50 px ahead, right 10 px, neither 30 px) past its ? crates, nitro
# walls and nitro field and the robot that chases it, without a death, to
# the room's exit (~frame 2460: InputCtrl::Update drops the camera lead and
# requests the exit, then SetLeadSpeed writes through the NULL lead, the
# NULL_WRITE), then on foot in the level's first room, where a TNT crate
# kills Crash (~2650) and he plays on from the start. The ride crashed the
# host on its first frame until SetLeadSpeed's NULL_WRITE and the camera
# lead's NULL_READs (its sprite has no bank).
# tools/boottest.py `screens` (the same --level and --room) played it on
# mGBA for tests/gem_path_mgba_screens.json: all 2900 frames the same.
# The ride was written by a search over the host's runs (each 12-frame
# step the one whose random continuations survived longest).
# A line `FRAME KEYS` holds KEYS from FRAME on (platform/pc/src/input.c).
